/*!
    \page reporting.html
    \title Reporting and Analysis
    \brief Analyze dashboard records with ReportEngine.

    ReportEngine inspects the supplied rows and classifies fields as numeric,
    date, Boolean, or text. It can filter records and generate grouped report
    rows using an aggregation.

    \section1 Basic Workflow

    1. Assign records to the \c rows property.
    2. Call \c analyze() to inspect available fields.
    3. Configure \c groupField, \c metricField, and \c aggregation.
    4. Add filters with \c setFilter().
    5. Call \c generateReport().
    6. Handle the \c reportGenerated(report) signal.

    \section1 Aggregations

    The reporting UI offers sum, average, count, minimum, and maximum
    aggregations. The selected aggregation is applied to the configured metric
    field for each group.

    \section1 Filters

    Use \c setFilter(field, operation, value, value2) to add or replace a
    filter for a field. Use \c removeFilter(field) to remove one filter, or
    \c clearFilters() to remove all filters.

    The exact supported operations are implemented in ReportEngine and should
    be checked against the current source when extending the reporting UI.
*/
